1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:03,080
You're leaving already, Lord Odin?

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,106
He may cause trouble,
but I'll still miss him.

3
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,717
I heard word there's a
monster living in Kuri.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,680
An ogre called Ashura Doji.

5
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,710
Hmm.

6
00:00:13,793 --> 00:00:14,886
Kuri's a blight on this land.

7
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:17,180
Even the Shogun cannot control it.

8
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:20,320
If the criminal takes refuge in Kuri,

9
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,897
the authorities are
powerless to apprehend him.

10
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:27,457
But if they lack the strength to survive
there, they'll be chewed up and spit out.

11
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:30,920
It's a lawless land almost
like a different country

12
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:37,880
Interesting, perhaps I should take a
tour around Wano have a safe trip Odin

13
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:42,440
Keen, Denjiro, come visit us again.

14
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:43,720
See ya.

15
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:49,300
He shows up uninvited and leaves just
as suddenly He values his freedom.

16
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:50,460
Lord Yasui

17
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,140
Come look, hurry

18
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:56,877
This is the room that Lord Odin stayed in.

19
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:58,977
Why on earth would he do such a thing?

20
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:01,648
We must send him a bill
for repairs at once.

21
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:06,080
Let's just pretend there
was a natural disaster.

22
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,735
If you're too soft on him,
he'll take advantage of you.

23
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:10,840
Lord Yasui!

24
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:12,800
What is it now?

25
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:16,460
The money is missing?

26
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,240
Yes, I'm certain I put it in
the safe, my lord. Um. Hmm?

27
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:28,280
It pains me dearly to say this But
I'm afraid that the money was stolen

28
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:33,977
I saw it It was Lord Odin
He slipped it into his

29
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:37,577
robe and walked away without
a word I knew it was that

30
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:40,097
scoundrel Biting the hand
that feeds him is what

31
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:43,900
he's doing He'll pay Would
Odin bother being sneaky?

32
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:47,400
Are you sure, Orochi?

33
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:49,740
Yes, forgive me

34
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:51,360
I was too afraid.

35
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:54,152
I should have made an effort to stop him.

36
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:07,980
After leaving Hakumai, Oden and his
followers continued onward to Kuri,

37
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:10,720
causing trouble all along the way.

38
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:20,957
How much longer are
you going to follow me?

39
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:21,960
Why forever?

40
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,671
Because we're your biggest fans, Lord Odin

41
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,020
He's annoyed

42
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:36,457
Hey, why are you standing
in the rain, you idiots?

43
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:40,834
As your retainers, we must protect
you Come on, you're going to get sick.

44
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:41,920
On our way!

45
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:45,348
What are you doing in here?

46
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:47,020
I am writing a journal.

47
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:49,460
They say it is a navigator's duty.

48
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:51,840
A daily observance on ships overseas.

49
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:57,172
The following are excerpts from Odin's
journal, chronicling his adventures.

50
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:11,780
in Ringo we met some ragged little
ruts a pair of starving siblings

51
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:15,920
get out of here

52
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,176
they tried to earn money by dancing
but people were as cold as the snow

53
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:33,120
Why do you little agents
keep following me?

54
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:36,240
That food isn't yours.

55
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:38,060
Are you listening?

56
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:39,420
Put that back.

57
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:42,881
They were the children of
a great master of dance.

58
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:46,197
But their families split apart
when their father was arrested.

59
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:50,740
They brazenly ate our Odin without
my permission, sobbing all the while.

60
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:52,580
Impossible to deter.

61
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:06,480
In Kibi, there was a goblin of a man who
cut the hair off the living and dead alike,

62
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:08,577
carrying it away into the night.

63
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:13,020
As it turns out, he sold brushes
made from human hair for a living.

64
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,160
Whoa! I give up! I give up!

65
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,297
I thought you were dead!

66
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:29,620
After I gave him a good wallop,
he strangely decided to follow me.

67
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:34,377
He claimed to be a long-suffering victim
of persecution, but he likely deserved it.

68
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:36,280
In the deep forests of Uda,

69
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:40,057
tales of a notorious mountain
bandit were carried on the wind.

70
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:43,552
They say he would abduct women
and beat men half to death.

71
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:46,700
Why are you following me, too?

72
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:47,900
Funny, right?

73
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:57,550
Hmm.

74
00:04:57,633 --> 00:04:58,967
Is that the mountain bandit?

75
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:03,760
You're okay!

76
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:08,360
In truth, the bandit was
a skilled ninja, Raizo,

77
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:13,160
who quit the Kozuki clan's Oniwabanshu
after Okunoichi broke his heart.

78
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:15,960
I can't live my life in hiding anymore!

79
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,612
Please take me with you!

80
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,240
He's annoyed!

81
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:37,660
Kozuki Oden came here?

82
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:39,700
He's the son of the shogun.

83
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:41,740
Killing him should be fun.

84
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:44,020
Go and bring him to me. Yes, sir!

85
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:57,440
More than anything, I love to see
the high and mighty brought low.

86
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:02,140
Hey, where did Odin go?

87
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,840
He went to take a dump,
I think. Been a while.

88
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:07,158
That was yesterday.

89
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:08,580
You know how he is.

90
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:12,197
He'll disappear for a day or two
on a whim with no explanation.

91
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:13,520
Uh, he went south.

92
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:15,577
Isn't there a gate to
Cootie south of here?

93
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:16,490
You're right!

94
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,240
Damn it all!

95
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,197
I told him I would die for him!

96
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:22,927
And then I let him sneak
off to battle alone!

97
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:57,420
The place I entered was
like a different world.

98
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:59,777
The stench of death filled the air,

99
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:04,160
and a violent wave thick like
blood seemed to aim itself at me.

100
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:08,980
Time to say goodbye to
your head, Kozuki Oden.

101
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:43,688
I've never been so proud of you
I've never been able to do it

102
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:48,657
Don't be a smile on your
birthday Oh, what do you say?

103
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:49,780
Shut it up!

104
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:53,220
You're not a soul

105
00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:03,817
you're in your mind You're not a

106
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:08,720
strength You're not a strength SAAA!

107
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,500
I've been disavowed!

108
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:05,920
I no longer have a name!

109
00:09:06,260 --> 00:09:10,440
Anyone can enter, but those who try
to leave will be promptly killed.

110
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,680
Especially samurai like you.

111
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:21,200
Sounds suffocating.

112
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:22,850
Huh?

113
00:09:22,933 --> 00:09:24,240
You've made a cage.

114
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:26,914
Watch in yourself when you can be free!

115
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,460
I didn't ask for your input.

116
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:34,157
You were foolish enough to come here,
so here you'll remain until your death.

117
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:36,220
which I expect will be imminent.

118
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:39,300
So no one can leave.

119
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:41,000
Now it's personal!

120
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:43,300
That's my least favorite rule!

121
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:45,860
It's my turf, so they're my rules!

122
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:47,780
Now die!

123
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:22,880
You run this hell home!

124
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:35,730
Odin!

125
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:38,240
We're coming!

126
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:40,152
Just stay where you are!

127
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,588
Look, he must have
broken through that gate!

128
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:55,560
This hellhole is the only
home that I will ever know!

129
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:59,420
A pampered bastard like you
could never understand my life!

130
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:03,160
Are you telling me this is
the life that you want?!

131
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:05,610
Look!

132
00:11:05,693 --> 00:11:06,540
He's up there!

133
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:08,700
Stop him!

134
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:20,650
Odin!

135
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:22,420
We'll help you fight!

136
00:11:25,980 --> 00:11:27,840
You're a moment too late.

137
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:30,880
I just wrapped up here. My apologies.

138
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:35,780
I fought all day and all
night, but it is done.

139
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:46,740
Why don't you kill me already?

140
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:49,840
I know there's no future for me.

141
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:52,680
I'll die with no regrets.

142
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:56,400
Is this Ashura Doji?

143
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:57,640
Their leader?

144
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:00,360
Listen to me, all of you.

145
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:04,000
Are you still willing to
follow me to the bitter end?

146
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:10,920
I need your aid, your strength, your wit.

147
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:16,200
For I have decided to lift up
the people of this cursed land

148
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:19,540
by becoming their king!

149
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:36,380
I come bearing news of young
Lord Odin What happened?

150
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:38,580
What did he do this time?

151
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:40,720
Take a look

152
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:47,640
Kuri has been tamed

153
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:54,900
Only Odin could accomplish this I
see it, but I can scarcely believe it

154
00:12:57,080 --> 00:13:01,760
The people of Kuri will ruff around the
edges but filled with boundless energy.

155
00:13:02,020 --> 00:13:05,017
Thanks to Odin's loyal companions
and headstrong leadership,

156
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:08,357
they turned their blood-soaked
land into a place worth living,

157
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:11,205
and the rest of Wano
could not help but notice.

158
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,600
In response to this accomplishment,

159
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:23,237
the shogun Kozuki Sukiyaki
retracted his disvowel

160
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:26,720
and instead gave his son
the title Daimyo of Kuri.

161
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:28,070
Look!

162
00:13:28,153 --> 00:13:31,022
Lord Odin is going to be
a dying yo for real now!

163
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:32,530
Yeah!

164
00:13:32,613 --> 00:13:34,377
Then Cootie will be a
full-fledged province!

165
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:35,460
We pulled it off!

166
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:37,522
All that hard work was worth it!

167
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:43,520
King's all right.

168
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:49,957
We knew you could do it
from the start, Lord Odin!

169
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:51,057
I'm so proud of you!

170
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:52,434
Congratulations, Odin!

171
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:54,914
Now Cootie will finally be your winner!

172
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,080
All right, friends!

173
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:06,180
I'm the Gaimyo!

174
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:07,890
Yeah!

175
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:21,000
You're looking dour, Asheran.

176
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:23,320
This is new to me.

177
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:24,910
I...

178
00:14:24,993 --> 00:14:27,140
I have never known peace before.

179
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:31,160
Thank you, Odin.

180
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:32,557
I owe you my...

181
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:33,660
Stop it!

182
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:34,980
You're creeping me!

183
00:14:38,820 --> 00:14:40,900
I was being sincere!

184
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:43,090
Huh?

185
00:14:43,173 --> 00:14:44,580
What are you doing? No!

186
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:49,070
Stop!

187
00:14:49,153 --> 00:14:50,577
You should be celebrating!

188
00:14:50,660 --> 00:14:53,920
You know, a proper Daimyo needs retainers.

189
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:58,140
I'm sure there are many
wise and prudent candidates.

190
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:02,700
But you're the only ones I want.

191
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:13,740
What say you?

192
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:15,400
Will you be my samurai?

193
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:40,940
No, it's not coming out of your noses!

194
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,000
No, it's on me!

195
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:43,940
Disgusting! Stop!

196
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:48,520
Six years passed in Wano without incident.

197
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:52,720
But across the seas, there
was a great storm brewing.

198
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:55,100
33 years before the present day,

199
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:59,777
the remnants of the legendary rocks
pirates began to form into their own crews,

200
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:04,684
with their strongest members becoming
infamous and influential in their own right.

201
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:13,520
What are they? Animals?

202
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:16,140
Just hairy men?

203
00:16:18,740 --> 00:16:21,000
What odd creatures they are.

204
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:28,980
Did you get it?

205
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:30,100
Think so?

206
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:37,900
Long ago,

207
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:40,300
several hundred years ago in fact,

208
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:45,337
the Minx and the Kozuki samurai
from the land of Wano made a pledge.

209
00:16:45,420 --> 00:16:49,760
We swore to be steadfast
allies through thick and thin.

210
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:51,500
Stupid waddo!

211
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:52,720
I hate it here!

212
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:54,280
Dear country, stop!

213
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:56,400
Get me down, dammit!

214
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:57,910
Help!

215
00:16:58,040 --> 00:16:59,500
I'm just a coppa!

216
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:00,816
You're all monsters!

217
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,637
We shouldn't have set
sail in the first place!

218
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:05,560
Coming here was a tough idea!

219
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:08,240
Some sworn allies you gotta are!

220
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:11,820
A cat monster, a dog
monster, and a coppa too.

221
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:14,337
I'm starting to feel like
this whole beach is cursed.

222
00:17:14,420 --> 00:17:15,600
Let's burn them!

223
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:27,452
This should be enough fish for the vinyl!

224
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:33,520
We're gonna die!

225
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:35,300
Help us!

226
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,780
Let them go!

227
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:47,940
Such cruelty!

228
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:49,360
Shame on you!

229
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:53,097
The only reason you fear them is
because they're different than you.

230
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:56,617
But those are children you bastards
tried to burn at the stake!

231
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:57,920
Thank you, Kara!

232
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:01,130
Farewell!

233
00:18:01,213 --> 00:18:03,022
You're just gonna leave us here!

234
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:12,920
Uh, why are there weird
little animals here?

235
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:14,100
They followed me.

236
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,900
Thank you, Grove, for rescuing us!

237
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:21,930
Hot!

238
00:18:22,260 --> 00:18:24,677
Yeah, we almost starved,
we almost drowned,

239
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:27,348
and then we almost got
burned to death, too!

240
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:28,650
Ah! Ah!

241
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:29,610
Damn it!

242
00:18:29,693 --> 00:18:31,068
This is way too hot to eat!

243
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:33,400
Yeah, no, this is unnatural.

244
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:36,016
They should not be talking like that.

245
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,240
Ah, delightful.

246
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:41,980
Father told me about minks like you.

247
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:42,970
Then I was right!

248
00:18:43,053 --> 00:18:46,277
I knew as soon as I saw that
symbol, we had it back home, too,

249
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,597
where they say our
nations are like brothers.

250
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:50,033
Yugaru saved our lives.

251
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:52,520
We were so hungry. Of course.

252
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:54,272
Eat as much as you like.

253
00:18:54,380 --> 00:18:55,620
Don't mind if I do.

254
00:18:57,140 --> 00:18:58,020
Like radish?

255
00:18:58,380 --> 00:18:59,740
You should try a bite.

256
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:01,587
It does look good, actually.

257
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:03,820
Now try the fish cake.

258
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:06,160
How is it?

259
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:07,820
It's too hot!

260
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:15,680
Yes, it's not sensitive to us, okay?

261
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:18,260
You've ruined it, you damn fool!

262
